draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117402","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117402","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117402.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117402.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-16T16:42:18Z"},"body":"- Helps address https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111218.\r\n- Follow-up to #117286.\r\n- Follow-up to #117295.\r\n- Follow-up to #117301.\r\n- Follow-up to #117328.\r\n- Follow-up to #117366.\r\n\r\n~I left out Jolt which @mihe will take a look at - its thirdparty includes should use angled brackets to remove warnings, and then there's a few actually unused/not directly used headers that can be cleaned up.~ *Edit:* Added in the end as it was trivial.\r\n\r\nI should have done the same for the OpenXR module as it turned out pretty hairy. `openxr_platform_inc.h` is horrifying, pulling a ton of platform specific stuff in headers when most of the time it just needs `vulkan.h` or some Metal header. I strongly recommend refactoring this further and decoupling OpenXR stuff as much as possible from platform-specific includes in headers. There also seems to be a pattern of including `openxr_api.h` and `openxr_util.h` everywhere even when not needed just to get `<openxr/openxr.h>` or a few other dependencies. These things add up and likely make recompile times pretty bad for folks working on OpenXR, so I advise you look into reducing the use of this pattern.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://a